            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59888",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "com.fasterxml.jackson.core/jackson-databind: tools.jackson.core/jackson-databind: jackson-databind: @JsonIgnore bypass in Java Records"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "jackson-databind contains the general-purpose data-binding functionality and tree-model for Jackson Data Processor. From 2.15.0 until 2.18.8, 2.21.4, and 3.1.4, Java Records using a PropertyNamingStrategy can bypass @JsonIgnore because POJOPropertiesCollector._removeUnwantedIgnorals() records an ignored component under its original implicit name before _renameUsing() applies the naming strategy, allowing the renamed JSON key to be assigned to the Record constructor parameter. This issue is fixed in versions 2.18.8, 2.21.4, and 3.1.4."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59888",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-59888\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind\nFixed Version: 2.18.8, 2.21.4\nLink: [CVE-2026-59888](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59888)\njackson-databind contains the general-purpose data-binding functionality and tree-model for Jackson Data Processor. From 2.15.0 until 2.18.8, 2.21.4, and 3.1.4, Java Records using a PropertyNamingStrategy can bypass @JsonIgnore because POJOPropertiesCollector._removeUnwantedIgnorals() records an ignored component under its original implicit name before _renameUsing() applies the naming strategy, allowing the renamed JSON key to be assigned to the Record constructor parameter. This issue is fixed in versions 2.18.8, 2.21.4, and 3.1.4.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-59888**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind|2.18.8, 2.21.4|[CVE-2026-59888](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59888)|\n\njackson-databind contains the general-purpose data-binding functionality and tree-model for Jackson Data Processor. From 2.15.0 until 2.18.8, 2.21.4, and 3.1.4, Java Records using a PropertyNamingStrategy can bypass @JsonIgnore because POJOPropertiesCollector._removeUnwantedIgnorals() records an ignored component under its original implicit name before _renameUsing() applies the naming strategy, allowing the renamed JSON key to be assigned to the Record constructor parameter. This issue is fixed in versions 2.18.8, 2.21.4, and 3.1.4."
              },
